  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Pherkad",
    "description": "Star in the constellation Ursa Minor",
    "summary": "Pherkad, Bayer designation Gamma Ursae Minoris, is a star in the northern constellation of Ursa Minor. Together with Beta Ursae Minoris (Kochab), it forms the end of the dipper pan of the \"Little Dipper\", which is an asterism forming the tail of the bear. Based upon parallax measurements obtained during the Hipparcos mission, it is approximately 487 light-years from the Sun.",
    "intro": "Pherkad , Bayer designation Gamma Ursae Minoris (γ Ursae Minoris, abbreviated Gamma UMi, γ UMi), is a star in the northern constellation of Ursa Minor. Together with Beta Ursae Minoris (Kochab), it forms the end of the dipper pan of the \"Little Dipper\", which is an asterism forming the tail of the bear. Based upon parallax measurements obtained during the Hipparcos mission, it is approximately 487 light-years (149 parsecs) from the Sun.",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pherkad",
